From fcdb60bf54b4fc1b889be800d1948787119d1c40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 09:26:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add Fund/LP ownership split, unfunded-commitment return,
 and bottom-up EV/EBITDA company model

Three Phase-1 gaps identified against a real secondaries pricing template:
- Fund vs. LP ownership: a secondary prices one LP's slice of the fund, not the
  whole fund. Every fund-level $ figure (cash flows, NAV, accrued carry, unfunded
  amounts) now scales to the selling LP's share at a single entry point, so the
  rest of the engine runs unchanged and ratios (DPI/RVPI/TVPI/IRR) stay correctly
  scale-invariant.
- Unfunded commitment generating its own return: build_unfunded_returns() projects
  a return (hold period + MOIC) on every future capital call, wired into both
  secondary_pricing() and leverage_overlay().
- Bottom-up EV/EBITDA company model: ebitda_exit_value() + implied_annual_return()
  let a portfolio company be modelled as Revenue -> EBITDA -> FCF -> Exit EV/EBITDA
  instead of a flat expected-return %, backing out an equivalent annualized return
  that plugs into the existing forecast_from_portfolio() unchanged.

Verified with 22 independent checks in test_v2_features.py (cross-checked by
manual arithmetic, not by re-calling the functions under test) plus a full
Streamlit AppTest smoke run across every new feature combination.

